cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use MAIL-Bench, please cite it as below."
title: "MAIL-Bench: Benchmarking Robotic Manipulation under Visual Availability Interruptions and Loss"
abstract: >-
  MAIL-Bench is a paired, closed-loop benchmark for the robustness of embodied
  manipulation policies under time-structured visual availability failures. On
  RoboCasa Atomic-Seen -- 18 tasks and 900 frozen scenes -- it asks whether a
  policy can solve a task with vision intact, at what phase of its own
  successful trajectory vision is lost, which functional visual role is lost and
  in what form, and how task success and completion efficiency change. It
  standardizes the evaluation and leaves model design and training method open.
